OverlayMain clips its children (overflow-hidden) and expects each settings
page to bring its own scroll container, like Connections and the
SettingsContent-based pages do. Account & usage was the only page without
one, so at short window heights the content simply cut off — hiding the
telemetry opt-out switch at the bottom with no way to reach it (owner
report, 2026-07-14). Wrap the page in the same overflow-y-auto wrapper
Connections uses.
